      -- local_taxes: $0.00
      -- mandatory_resort_or_city_charge: $0.00
      -- parking_cost: $0.00
      -- no_compliant_accommodation_available_evidenced: true
    }
  assertion r.applicable_cap = $308.00
  assertion r.accommodation_reimbursable = $150.00
```

## E4_3_TaxesAndCityChargeCountAgainstTheCap

E-4.3: a £210 room with £15 of local taxes and a £10 mandatory city charge is
£235 against a £220 cap, so £220 is reimbursed — not the £210 room rate.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE4_3_TaxesAndCityChargeCountAgainstTheCap:
  output r content Accommodation.NightlyAccommodation

scope TestE4_3_TaxesAndCityChargeCountAgainstTheCap:
  definition r equals
    output of Accommodation.NightlyAccommodation with {
      -- city_tier: ExpenseDefs.CityTier.Tier1
      -- room_cost: $210.00
      -- local_taxes: $15.00
      -- mandatory_resort_or_city_charge: $10.00
      -- parking_cost: $0.00
      -- no_compliant_accommodation_available_evidenced: false
    }
  assertion r.cost_against_cap = $235.00
  assertion r.accommodation_reimbursable = $220.00
  assertion r.reimbursable_amount = $220.00
```

## E4_3_TaxesExactlyReachTheCap

